.TH CONDENSE 1 "2025-06-28" "1.0.1" "Condense Manual"
.SH NAME
condense \- high-performance CLI proxy that filters command output to save AI tokens
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B condense
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B condense gain
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B condense doctor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B condense explain
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B condense read
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.br
.B condense init
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B condense config
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B condense mcp
[\fI\-\-start\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B condense
is a CLI proxy that sits between your AI coding assistant and the shell.
It intercepts commands, executes the real binary, filters the output using
one of 12 compression strategies, and returns a compact summary to the AI
context window \- saving 60\-90% of tokens on typical workloads.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-vv ", " \-vvv
Increase verbosity. \fB\-v\fR shows normal summary with more detail,
\fB\-vv\fR includes file lists, \fB\-vvv\fR shows maximum verbosity.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-ultra\-compact
Maximum compression: single\-line ASCII icon output.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format for a proxied command: \fBtext\fR (default) or \fBjson\fR.
Must come before the proxied command
(\fBcondense \-\-format json pytest\fR).
JSON waits until the child exits and prints one schema\-1 document.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Print help text and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B condense gain
Show token savings analytics. See
.BR "condense gain \-\-help"
for options including \fB\-\-graph\fR, \fB\-\-history\fR, \fB\-\-top N\fR,
\fB\-\-scope project\fR, and \fB\-\-format json\fR.
.TP
.B condense doctor
Diagnose persistence, hooks, and empty analytics. Use
\fBcondense doctor \-\-format json\fR for a machine-readable report.
.TP
.B condense explain
Show which filter stages dropped or rewrote output, with line and token
accounting. Options must come before the command
(\fBcondense explain \-\-format json pytest\fR).
Use \fB\-\-input FILE\fR to explain a captured fixture without executing.
.TP
.B condense read
Read a source file with comment-strip or structural outline. Line numbers
map to the original file. Options must come before the path
(\fBcondense read \-\-level comments Src.java\fR).
Unknown languages stay verbatim. JSON is never treated as C.
.TP
.B condense init
Install AI tool hooks (fallback; MCP is preferred). Use \fBcondense init \-g\fR
to install for all supported tools, \fBcondense init \-\-show\fR to check status
and integrity, \fBcondense init \-\-remove\fR to uninstall. Tools include
Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini, Windsurf, Copilot, Cline, Codex, OpenCode,
Kilo, Antigravity, Hermes, and Pi. Matched commands are denied with a retry
message; they are never rewritten and auto-allowed.
.TP
.B condense config
Read and write Condense configuration. Use \fBcondense config \-\-list\fR,
\fBcondense config \-\-get KEY\fR, \fBcondense config \-\-set KEY=VALUE\fR,
or \fBcondense config \-\-reset\fR.
.TP
.B condense mcp
Print an MCP client snippet, or start the stdio JSON-RPC server with
\fBcondense mcp \-\-start\fR. Tools are \fBrun\fR, \fBexplain\fR, and
\fBread\fR. Resources are \fBcondense://gain\fR and \fBcondense://doctor\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Filter git status:
.B condense git status
.TP
Filter cargo test output (failures only):
.B condense cargo test
.TP
Filter pytest (failures + summary):
.B condense pytest
.TP
Ultra-compact mode:
.B condense \-u git status
.TP
Verbose mode (includes file list):
.B condense \-vv git status
.TP
Show token savings dashboard:
.B condense gain
.TP
30\-day savings graph:
.B condense gain \-\-graph
.TP
Start the MCP server on stdio:
.B condense mcp \-\-start
.TP
Install AI tool hooks:
.B condense init \-g
.TP
Show config:
.B condense config \-\-list
.SH SUPPORTED COMMANDS
git, cargo, pytest, go test, npm, jest, vitest, eslint, tsc, ruff,
docker, kubectl, aws, ls, grep, rg, find, cat, make, mvn, gradle,
pip install, golangci\-lint, and more.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/condense/config.toml
User configuration file (Linux/XDG).
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application\ Support/condense/config.toml
User configuration file (macOS).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/condense/condense.db
SQLite analytics database (Linux/XDG).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/condense/tee/
Directory where raw command output is saved on failure.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Condense propagates the exit code of the proxied command verbatim. If git status
exits 128 (not a git repository), condense also exits 128.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR cargo (1),
.BR pytest (1)
